<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.draft.stages ~ the first of memory's two crossings: a local row a lift later names

`kahua stage <title>` writes ONE row into the face's local canon `bags/daemon-<F>`: local to this device, unsigned, and it lifts nothing. The operator's hand carries a staged row to the fleet with `lares kahua lift <title>`, reading its preview first. `text` carries the row's whole body; `fields` carries its string-valued fields (`title`, `text` and any `kahua-` field never ride). A row already standing at the title gives way to this one.

The answer is {title, digest, relation, staged}. `digest` names the ROW digest (sha-256 over the body and the carried fields), the one a lift's `--digest` takes, never the BODY digest a proposal carries (`face.draft.proposes`); `staged` reads false where the row already stood at that digest and nothing moved. The terminal prints the same note on stderr beside the door's JSON. A face with no local canon standing refuses `kahua-stage-no-canon`. The seat's tool rides a `seat` session over the @daemon wire.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ a-row · a-row-with-fields · on-a-named-face

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-row` params=`title/T text/<body> ~ stage one row from a body on the line`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-row-with-fields` params=`title/T text/<body> fields/<fields> ~ carry string-valued fields beside the body`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`on-a-named-face` params=`title/T text/<body> face/1 ~ stage into one face's local canon`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ title · text · file · fields · face

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`title` params=`takes/title needs/required seat/1 as/<title> ~ the row's title`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`text` params=`takes/body ~ the row's whole body; the terminal names it by --text or --file (one of them), the seat's tool by text`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`file` params=`takes/path skins/cli ~ the terminal's other way to name the body: a file the door reads`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`fields` params=`takes/json-object ~ the row's string-valued fields (an object of strings on the seat, JSON on the terminal); 'title', 'text' and any 'kahua-' field never ride`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/handle-index ~ any face inside the lent set, by persona index (a whole number from 0); absent, the worn face; a face outside the set refuses 'face-not-lent', a shut one 'face-not-open'`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ seat-or-hand

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`seat-or-hand` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ a local, unsigned row on this device alone, in the face's local canon bags/daemon-<F>; any seat may stage, and a lift (the hand's act) is what carries it to the fleet`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ kahua-stage-text · kahua-stage-no-canon · fields-malformed · face-not-lent · face-not-open

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`kahua-stage-text` params=`cure/[[face.draft.stages title/T text/<body>]] ~ name the row's body by text or file, one of them, never both`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`kahua-stage-no-canon` params=`~ the face stands no local canon to stage into`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`fields-malformed` params=`cure/[[face.draft.stages title/T text/<body> fields/<fields>]] ~ fields needs JSON on the terminal, an object of string values on the seat`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`face-not-lent` params=`~ the face stands outside the lent set the seat may name`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`face-not-open` params=`~ the face stands shut; open it first`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ staged · unchanged

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`staged` params=`exit/0 fields/[[title digest relation staged]] ~ the row stands in the face's local canon at the row digest`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`unchanged` params=`exit/0 ~ staged reads false: the row already stood at that digest and nothing moved`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

